***	The original rules are combined into a single unconditional rule using an if-then-else expression. This improves efficiency by reducing the number of rule-matching attempts and ensuring the parity check (N rem 2) is evaluated only once per transition. The implementation preserves the original semantics, including the behavior for N=0 and the termination cycle for N=1, while adhering to the function signatures (Nat to Nat) and using standard Maude notation.
***	</comment>
***

mod COLLATZ is
	protecting NAT .

	*** Collatz conjecture
	*** (no one has proven that this sequence is always terminating)

	var N : Nat .

	rl N => if N rem 2 == 0 then N quo 2 else 3 * N + 1 fi .
endm